-- title:
--   q-expansion field of X(Γ) embeds into level-M modular functions
-- statement:
--   Let $M\ge 1$, let $\Gamma\le \mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z})$ be a subgroup containing the principal congruence subgroup $\Gamma(M)$ and the translation $T=\begin{pmatrix}1&1\\0&1\end{pmatrix}$, and let $\iota\colon\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\to\mathbb{C}$ be a ring homomorphism, where $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}=$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`. Let $A_M=$ [`ModularCurve.LevelN.ring M`](def/ModularCurve_LevelNFunctionField.html#L28) be the $\mathbb{C}$-subalgebra of $\mathbb{H}\to\mathbb{C}$ generated by $j=E_4^3/\Delta$ together with the functions `fricke M v` for the nonzero $v\in(\mathbb{Z}/M)^2$, and let $K$ be a field which is simultaneously a $\mathbb{C}$-algebra and an $A_M$-algebra compatibly, and is a fraction field of $A_M$. Write $F=$ [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of [`ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ Γ`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L101): the subfield of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ generated over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ by the coefficientwise images of the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the quotients $p_f/p_g$, for $f,g$ modular forms of a common weight on $\Gamma$ (viewed in $\mathrm{GL}(2,\mathbb{R})$) with integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g$, $p_g\neq 0$. Then there is a ring homomorphism $\Phi\colon F\to K$ such that: $\Phi$ sends each constant $c\in\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ to the image of $\iota(c)$ in $K$; every element of $F$ whose underlying Laurent series is [`ModularCurve.jqModC`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L15) over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, namely $q^{-1}$ times the image of the integral power series $E_4^3\eta^{-24}$, is sent to the image of $j\in A_M$ in $K$; and the image of $\Phi$ is fixed by $\Gamma$ in the following sense: for every $\gamma\in\Gamma$, assuming $A_M$ is stable under $G\mapsto G(\gamma^{-1}\cdot{-})$, any $\mathbb{C}$-algebra automorphism $\varphi$ of $K$ acting on elements of $A_M$ by that substitution satisfies $\varphi(\Phi u)=\Phi u$ for all $u\in F$.
--
--   This is the arithmetic specialisation step identifying the $q$-expansion function field of $X(\Gamma)$ with a subfield of the field $\mathbb{C}(X(M))=\mathbb{C}(j,f_v)$ of modular functions of level $M$, compatibly with $j$ and with the action of $\Gamma$ by fractional linear substitutions. It is used in the counting arguments that compare the number of fibres of `jqModC`, respectively places of the base-changed field, with the number of double cosets, and hence in the computation of degrees and indices for modular curves.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_ringHom_laurentBaseChange_qExpFunctionFieldC_levelN.lean

